$DATUM 4-tert-Butyloxycarbonyl-(4-tert-butyloxycarbonylaminobutyl)aminobutanal
(10). Bis acetoxyiodobenzene (1.1 equiv, 1.1 mmol) and
2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidine-1-oxyl (0.1 equiv, 0.1 mmol) were added to
a stirring solution of aminoalcohol 14 (1 equiv, 1 mmol) in
dichloromethane (1 mL) at r.t. for 5 h under Ar. Dichloromethane was
added and the organic solution was washed with saturated aqueous Na2S2O3,
NaHCO3, brine, and water. The organic extracts were dried over Na2SO4,
filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure; and the residue was
purified by chromatography on silica gel (CH2Cl2/EtOAc: (8:2)). Compound
9 as a colorless oil (75%). IR (film): γ = 2974, 2930, 2867, 1694, 1479,
1390, 1168 cm-1. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ = 1.35-1.62 (m, 22H, CH 2CH 2
and 2 C(CH 3)3), 1.83 (qt, 2H, 3 J = 7.1 Hz, CH 2 3), 2.44 (t, 2H, 3 J =
7.1 Hz, CH 2 2), 3.04-3.27 (m, 6H), 4.56 (br s, 1H, NH), 9.77 (s, 1H,
CHO) ppm. 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz): δ = 21.2 (CH2), 25.8 (CH2), 27.6
(CH2), 28.5 (C(CH3)3), 28.6 (C(CH3)3), 40.3 (CH2), 41.2 (CH2),46.3 (CH2),
46.8 (CH2), 79.3 (C(CH3)3), 79.7 (C(CH3)3), 155.7 (C=O), 156.1 (C=O),
201.7 (CHO) ppm. HRMS (MALDI): calcd. for C18H34NaN2O5 [M+Na]+; 381.2360;
found 381.2366.
