$DATUM Synthesis of aldehyde 17 To a solution of diol 11 (22.1 g, 170 mmol, 1.0
equiv) in CH2Cl2 (500 mL) was added 2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidinooxy
(7.96 g, 51.0 mmol, 0.3 equiv), (diacetoxyiodo)benzene (71.2 g, 221.0
mmol, 1.3 equiv) at room temperature. The solution was stirred at the
room temperature for 5 h before being quenched by the addition of
saturated aqueous Na2S2O3 (300 mL). The organic layers were separated,
and the aqueous layers were extracted with ether (3 x 200 mL). The
combined organic phase was dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated
under reduced pressure. Purification of the crude product by flash column
chromatography on silica gel (hexane/ethyl acetate = 5/1). Aldehyde 17
(16.4 g, 75% yield) as a colorless oil. Rf = 0.7 (hexane/ethyl acetate =
2/1); IR (film) λmax 2972, 2929, 1093, 925, 798 cm-1; 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 9.61 (s, 1H), 5.99 - 5.81 (m, 1H), 5.33 (t, J = 14.2 Hz, 2H),
4.32 (d, J = 6.2 Hz, 1H), 2.35(b, 1H), 1.12 (s, 3H), 1.08 (s, 3H); 13C
NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 205.5, 134.8, 117.0, 75.5, 48.9, 18.3, 15.2; HRMS
(ESI) calcd for C7H13O2 [M+H]+ 129.0910; found: 129.0910.
