$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of
5-methyl-5-(3-methyl-hexa-3,5-dienyl)-cyclopent)-cyclopent-1-enecarb-aldehyde
(17): To a solution of the alcohol made above in CH2Cl2 (25 mL) was added
BAIB (925 mg, 2.87 mmol) and TEMPO (45 mg, 0.29 mmol) at 0 °C, and the
formed mixture was then warmed up 30 °C, and continually stirred for 12
h. The reaction was worked up by removal of the solvent, and the residue
was purified by a flash chromatography on silica gel (PE/ethyl acetate =
40/1) to give 17 (430 mg) in 75% yield. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, ppm): δ
1.26 (s, 3H), 1.68-1.87 (m, 7H), 1.96-2.06 (m, 2H), 2.49-2.56 (m, 2H),
4.94-4.98 (dd, J1 = 10.2 Hz, J2 = 1.8 Hz, 1H), 4.98-5.11 (dd, J1 = 10.8
Hz, J2 = 2.1 Hz, 1H), 5.82-5.85 (d, J = 10.8 Hz, 1H), 6.49-6.62 (m, 1H),
6.78-6.81 (t, 1H), 9.75 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3, ppm): δ 16.8,
25.6, 28.1, 31.2, 35.4, 37.1, 37.6, 114.5, 125.1, 133.3, 139.8, 152.5,
154.3, 189.9; HRMS m/z calcd for C14H20O [M+] 204.1514, found [M+]
204.1516.
