$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM γ-Hydroxylactone 70. To a solution of lactol 68 (12 mg, 14.5 umol) and
TEMPO (45 mg, 0.29 mmol) in acetonitrile (1.5 mL) was added bisacetoxy
iodobenzene (93 mg, 0.29 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at 25 °C
until TLC indicated complete consumption of starting material (ca 2 h).
The reaction was quenched by addition of a saturated aqueous NaHCO3
solution (5 mL) and extracted with ether (3x5 mL). The combined organic
extracts were washed with water (10 mL) and brine (10 mL), and then dried
(MgSO4) and concentrated. The residue was purified by flash column
chromatography (silica gel, hexanes:EtOAc, 7:1→2:1) to furnish
y-hydroxylactone 70 as a clear thick oil (8.8 mg, 74%). 70: Rf= 0.55
(silica gel, hexanes:EtOAc, 2:1); IR (neat) vmax 3402, 2929, 2856, 1769,
1714, 1463, 1261,1096, 966 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.01 (d, J =
2.5 Hz, 1 H), 5.49-5.30 (m, 5 H, includes D20 exchangeable -OH), 4.65 (t,
J = 6.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.07 (d, J = 10.0 Hz, 1 H), 3.93 (d, J = 10.0 Hz, 1 H),
3.52 (s, 1 H), 2.88-2.74 (m, 3 H), 2.59 (dt, J = 18.0, 7.0 Hz, 1 H),
2.37-2.19 (m, 3 H), 2.07-1.90 (m, 4 H), 1.71-1.58 (m, 10 H), 1.48-1.04
(m, 10 H), 0.98-0.91 (m, 18 H), 0.63 (q, J = 8.0 Hz, 6 H), 0.19 (s, 3 H),
0.18 (s, 3 H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 212.6, 174.8, 165.1, 165.0,
144.3, 140.6, 136.8, 133.3, 131.3, 129.7, 125.7, 124.8, 104.3, 74.4,
53.9, 41.4, 40.7, 40.1, 37.9, 37.4, 33.1, 32.4, 29.6, 29.0, 27.8, 26.1,
25.6, 18.0, 17.9, 6.7, 4.2, -4.3, -4.8; HRMS (MALDI) calcd for
C42H66O9Si2Na+ [M + Na+] 793.4138, found 793.4112.
