$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 1-hydroxy-6-oxo-cyclohex-2-encarboxylate [(-)-2]. To a stirred
solution of methyl 1,6-dihydroxy-cyclohex-2-encarboxylate (50 mg, 0.29
mmol) and AZADO (4.4 mg, 0.029 μmol) in CH2Cl2 (0.58 mL) was added
PS-BAIB (234 mg). After stirring for 5 min, the reaction mixture was
quenched with iPrOH (0.4 mL) and diluted with Et2O. The mixture was
filtered thorough filter paper and filter paper was washed with Et2O. The
combined filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure. The resulting
residue was purified by silica gel column chromatography (AcOEt : Hexane
= 1 : 1) to give methyl 1-hydroxy-6-oxo-cyclohex-2-encarboxylate (70.7
mg, 71%) as a colorless oil. Methyl
1-hydroxy-6-oxo-cyclohex-2-encarboxylate [(-)-2], yield 70.7 mg, 71%.
[α]D27 -274.8°(c 1.01, CHCl3); FT-IR (neat) ν 3465, 2957, 1748, 1725,
1437, 1359, 1259, 1138, 1102 cm-1; 1H-NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.12 (1H,
dt, J = 9.7, 3.9 Hz), 5.79 (1H, ddd, J = 9.7, 1.7 Hz), 4.18 (1H, s), 3.80
(3H, s), 3.00 (1H, dt, J = 14.3, 8.0 Hz), 2.75 (1H, m), 2.66 (1H, m),
2.58 (1H, m); 13C-NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 205.4, 170.4, 131.8, 127.7,
78.0, 53.4, 35.1, 26.9; MS (EI) m/z : 170 (M +), 128 (100%); HRMS (EI)
calcd for C8H10O4: 170.0579, found: 170.0560; Anal. Calcd. for C8H10O4 :
C, 56.47. H, 5.92. Found : C, 56.17. H, 5.90.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, solid-supported reagent (polystyrene-supported BAIB used)
