$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1.4 Catalytic oxidation of alcohol 0.25 mmol
α-phenylethanol was dissolved in 1 mL solvent followed by the addition of
0.35 mmol oxygen source PhI(OAc)2 and 2 mol% catalyst. The mixture was
stirred at room temperature for 1 h. After the reaction was complete,
column chromatography was used to remove the catalyst (eluent : ethyl
acetate). HP 6890GC/MS5973 gas chromatograph mass spectrometer was
applied for qualitative analysis, and HP 6890 gas chromatograph (OV-17
capillary column) for quantitative analysis. ortho-chloroacetophenone, 71
%
