$DATUM Synthesis of
4-[5-methyl-5-(3-methyl-hexa-3,5-dienyl)-cyclopent-1-enyl]-4-oxo-but-2-ynoic
acid ethyl ester (10): To a solution of ethyl propriolate (300 mg, 3.05
mmol) in dry THF (2 mL) was added a LDA solution [prepared from n-BuLi
(1.0 mL, 2.5 M in hexane) and i-Pr2NH (0.36 mL) in THF(15 mL)] at - 78 °C
under nitrogen. After stirring at -78 °C for 1 h, the mixture was warmed
up to 0 °C, and compound 17 (400 mg, 2 mmol) in THF (3 mL) was added, and
reaction mixture was then stirred at room temperature for 30 min. The
reaction was quenched with a saturated solution of NH4Cl (10 mL), and the
mixture was then extracted with Et2O (3 x 30 mL). The combined extracts
were first washed with brine (2 x 10 mL), and then dried over Na2SO4. The
solvent was removed under vacuum, and the residue was purified by a flash
chromatography on silica gel (PE/ethyl acetate = 8/1) to give the adduct
(590 mg) in 98% yield.which was then dissolved in CH2Cl2 (10 mL), and
then treated with TEMPO (17 mg, 0.11 mmol) and BAIB (350 mg, 1.1 mmmol)
at 0 °C, and the formed mixture was then warmed to 30 °C and stirred
overnight. After removal of the solvent under vacuum, the residue was
purified by a flash chromatography on silica gel (PE/ethyl acetate =
30/1) to give compound 10 (410 mg) in 70% yield. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3,
ppm): δ 1.26 (s, 3H), 1.32-1.34 (t, 3H), 1.64-1.90 (m, 7H), 1.94-2.01 (m,
2H), 2.52-2.59 (m, 2H), 4.27-4.35 (q, 2H), 4.95-4.99 (dd, J1 = 10.2 Hz,
J2 = 1.8 Hz, 1H), 5.05-5.11 (dd, J1 = 17.1 Hz, J2 = 2.1 Hz, 1H),
5.81-5.84 (d, J = 10.8 Hz, 1H), 6.49-6.62 (m, 1H), 7.20-7.21 (t, 1H); 13C
NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3, ppm): δ 13.9, 16.7, 25.6, 31.4, 35.3, 36.9, 37.4,
49.0, 62.8, 80.1, 114.6, 125.3, 133.3, 139.5, 151.0, 152.5, 155.0, 173.2;
HRMS m/z calcd for C19H24O3 [M+] 300.1725, found [M+] 300.1727.
