$DATUM To a solution of compound 19 (240 mg, 0.8 mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (25 mL)
were added TEMPO (25 mg, 0.16 mmol) and diacetoxyiodobenzene (773 mg, 2.4
mmol) at 0 °C and it was allowed to stir for 10 h. at room temperature.
CH2Cl2 was concentrated and directly transferred into a silica gel column
and purified (3% EtOAc/hexane) to obtain aldehyde. Yield 168 mg (70%).
