$DATUM Aldehyde 31. (Diacetoxyiodo)benzene (BAIB) (11.5 g, 35.7 mmol) was added
to a solution of alcohol 30 (9.2 g, 32.4 mmol) and
(2,2,6,6-Tetramethylpiperidinin-1-yl)oxyl (TEMPO) (515 mg, 3.3 mmol) in
anhydrous CH2Cl2 (92 mL). The reaction mixture was stirred at 23 ºC for
20 h then was quenched with a saturated aqueous solution of NH4Cl (100
mL) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 100 mL). The combined organic layers
were dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated. The residue
was purified by flash chromatography (Hexane/EtOAc 5:1 to 4:1). 31 (6.3
g, 70% yield) as colourless oil. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ: 9.78 (s, 1H),
7.25 (d, 2H, J = 8.7 Hz), 6.85 (d, 2H, J = 8.7 Hz), 5.64 (t, 1H, J = 7.8
Hz), 4.45 (q, 2H, J = 11.1 Hz), 4.02 (m, 1H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 2.60 (m, 2H),
2.35 (m, 2H), 2.03 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz) δ: 201.0, 159.6,
132.1, 130.1, 129.7, 122.8, 114.1, 73.3, 71.5, 55.5, 48.3, 33.5, 21.3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Isolation and First Total Synthesis of PM050489 and PM060184, Two New
Marine Anticancer Compounds
