$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: γ-Hydroxylactone 70. To a solution of lactol
68 (12 mg, 14.5 umol) and TEMPO (45 mg, 0.29 mmol) in acetonitrile (1.5
mL) was added bisacetoxy iodobenzene (93 mg, 0.29 mmol). The reaction
mixture was stirred at 25 °C until TLC indicated complete consumption of
starting material (ca 2 h). The reaction was quenched by addition of a
saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution (5 mL) and extracted with ether (3x5
mL). The combined organic extracts were washed with water (10 mL) and
brine (10 mL), and then dried (MgSO4) and concentrated. The residue was
purified by flash column chromatography (silica gel, hexanes:EtOAc,
7:1→2:1) to furnish y-hydroxylactone 70 as a clear thick oil (8.8 mg,
74%). Lactone 73. Lactol 73 was prepared from bis-lactol 72 according to
the same procedure used to prepare 70 from 68 (72, 3.7 mg, 0.0046
mmol→73, 2.6 mg, 70% yield). colorless oil. 73: Rf = 0.43 (silica gel,
EtOAc:hexane 1:4); IR (film) νmax 3416, 2956, 2928, 2855,1836, 1768,
1466, 1427, 1385, 1260, 1172, 1109, 1006, 967, 817, 740, 703 cm-1; 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 7.77-7.69 (m, 4 H), 7.48-7.41 (m, 6 H), 6.07 (d, J =
3.5 Hz, 1 H), 5.73 (s, 1 H), 5.39-5.30 (m, 2 H), 4.12-4.06 (m, 1 H), 4.09
(d, J = 10 Hz, 1 H), 3.99 (d, J = 10 Hz, 1 H), 3.96-3.88 (m, 1 H), 3.93
(s, 1 H), 2.97 (d, J = 19.0 Hz, 1 H), 2.86 (d, J = 19.0 Hz, 1 H),
2.65-2.58 (m, 1 H), 2.13-2.05 (m, 1 H), 1.98-1.82 (m, 2 H), 1.82-1.75 (m,
1 H), 1.71-1.11 (m, 11 H), 1.64 (d, J = 3.5 Hz, 3 H), 1.07 (s, 9 H), 0.98
(t, J = 8.0 Hz, 9 H), 0.65 (q, J = 8:0 Hz, 6 H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3)
δ = 174.9,.165.6, 164.8, 144.6, 140.3, 137.6, 135.7 (2 C), 133.0, 132.7,
131.2, 130.1, 130.0, 127.9 (4 C), 124.8, 105.0, 62.9, 61.8, 52.5, 48.6,
42.6, 38.7, 37.5, 35.9, 33.5, 32.4, 29.5, 29.0, 27.5, 26.8 (2 C), 19.1,
17.9, 6.7 (3 C), 4.2 (3 C); HRMS (FAB) calcd for C46H62O8Si2Cs [M + Cs+]
931.3038, found 931.3063.
